# Start With Current Database

```sh
docker compose up -d --build
```

## Holdsport

Set `HOLDSPORT_USERNAME`, `HOLDSPORT_PASSWORD`, and `HOLDSPORT_TEAM_ID` in
`.env`. The team ID is required so the worker can verify that Holdsport switched
to the correct team. `HOLDSPORT_SQUAD_ID` selects the local squad that receives
the integration.

Create separate active fine rules for Holdsport training and matches. Set each
amount and the number of days, hours, and minutes before activity start in the
administrator panel. Grant `Holdsport` permission to administrators who should
see RSVP data.

The `holdsport-cron` service checks every minute and applies a rule as soon as
its configured lead time is reached. It refreshes the full RSVP overview hourly.
Repeated runs are safe and never fine Holdsport rows marked as coaches.

The Holdsport overview shows the fine created for each participant. Administrators
can map unmatched Holdsport names directly to active players, remove every fine
created by one activity, or fetch the current RSVP list and replace that activity's
old fines by retriggering it. A manual trigger uses the current active season when
the future activity is outside the season's configured dates.
